sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor P as Player
  participant App
  participant RLS as PostgREST/RLS
  participant DB as Postgres functions
  participant Cal as Calendar app (Apple / Google / Outlook)
  participant V as Vercel api/calendar.ts
  P->>App: Settings → Calendar sync → Subscribe
  App->>RLS: rpc rotate_calendar_feed() (authenticated)
  RLS->>DB: SECURITY DEFINER, user = auth.uid()
  DB-->>App: token (uuid) — upserted into calendar_feeds
  App->>Cal: open webcal://vteamvolleyball.com/cal/<token>.ics
  loop every ~1–24h (client decides)
    Cal->>V: GET /cal/<token>.ics
    V->>RLS: rpc calendar_feed(p_token) with anon key
    RLS->>DB: SECURITY DEFINER: look up token → user_id
    DB-->>V: {ok, events[]} attending / waitlisted / hosting / co-hosting,<br/>−30d … +180d, cancelled ones flagged (touch last_fetched_at ≤ hourly)
    V-->>Cal: 200 text/calendar (VEVENT per event, UID event-<id>@vteam,<br/>STATUS CONFIRMED / TENTATIVE / CANCELLED), s-maxage=900
  end
  Note over Cal,V: Unknown or revoked token → 404 (calendar stops updating)
  P->>App: Reset link
  App->>RLS: rpc rotate_calendar_feed() → new token, old URL 404s
